id: E2185-draft-2301_80739235
draft: true
title: "Library-only CMake packages must reconstruct unregistered upstream self-checks"
category: cmake, conan, upstream-tests, inventory, library-only, ohos
match_keywords: >
  CMake utility targets, no add_test, zero CTest registrations,
  no-argument self-check, fixture-required utility, library-only package,
  removed test subdirectory, installed static library, upstream denominator
root_cause: >
  Some CMake projects call a directory test/ but only create command-line
  executables there and never register them with CTest. A library-only package
  may correctly remove that subdirectory from its install build, yet treating
  zero CTest registrations as zero upstream tests can hide deterministic
  no-argument self-check programs. Counting every utility is also wrong because
  data converters and analyzers can require external files that the release
  archive does not supply as test fixtures.
error_signature: >
  No tests were found|CTest registration count.*0|add_executable.*test/|
  add_subdirectory\("?test|Usage:.*<.*file|library-only.*upstream tests
trigger_tool: cmake, ctest, conan, target-runner
phase: upstream-inventory, package-build, target-validation, pre-pr
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Inventory CTest registrations and executable targets independently. Inspect
  each executable's entry point and required inputs, classify deterministic
  no-argument self-checks separately from fixture-required utilities, and keep
  the production package library-only. Rebuild only the eligible unchanged
  upstream sources against the installed package in a target transaction, then
  sign and execute them with per-program return-code and output evidence. Report
  zero CTest registrations, the eligible N/N result, excluded utility names and
  reasons, and the package consumer as separate denominators.
rec_command: >
  inspect test/CMakeLists.txt for add_executable and add_test; compile each
  no-argument self-check against the installed library; sign target ELFs; run
  each once and require all return codes to be zero
verification_cmd: >
  require CTEST_REGISTERED=0, a source-bound eligible inventory, N/N PASS for
  every eligible self-check, explicit exclusion reasons for all other utility
  targets, and an independently passing package consumer
affected_scope: >
  C or C++ libraries whose upstream CMake test directories contain a mixture
  of internal self-check executables and command-line data utilities, especially
  when downstream packaging intentionally omits those utilities from install.
safety_boundary: >
  Do not infer a test from a directory or target name alone, count a usage/error
  exit as PASS, invent missing fixtures, or replace a complete registered test
  suite with a selected executable subset. Reconstructed checks must use
  unchanged upstream sources, the installed package, a runnable target, and
  exact per-program evidence; consumer assertions remain a separate scope.
